      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SMART MISSION (1) has the best recent form, finishing fourth in a Class 3 at this track, just three lengths behind and well-backed. A stronger reference is his Townsville second to Heart Of Vienna last time, where he was beaten a nose after being checked around the 800m. The drop to BM55 third-up suits him. NOSEY NEO (8) is the biggest threat, showing consistency with a Cooktown third and an Innisfail second in his last two outings. He steps up from picnic racing, but a return to a winning distance, weight relief, and first-time blinkers bolster his chances. CATCH A BREAK (5) returns after six months, bringing mixed Victorian form, including a decent Swan Hill sixth. His 1250m record dampens win expectations, but he has enough to be competitive fresh. DIAMOND LUCY (6) was disappointing in a last-start Class 5 at Townsville, but her previous BM62 win against Singular makes her a contender if she returns to that form.",
